VeridianOS: KirigamiAddons date and time: types.h is Android-only

src/dateandtime/types.h declares its one QML type (the Android
integration singleton, a Q_GADGET) inside #ifdef Q_OS_ANDROID; elsewhere
it declares nothing. It was a source of the plugin on every platform, so
AutoMoc ran moc on it, which outside Android found nothing:
"types.h: note: No relevant classes found. No output generated." It is
now added to the plugin only when building for Android, next to that
platform's other sources. Nothing changes on Android, and elsewhere the
plugin had no type from it.

--- a/src/dateandtime/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/dateandtime/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -32,8 +32,12 @@
     yearmodel.cpp
     monthmodel.cpp
     infinitecalendarviewmodel.cpp
-    types.h
 )
+
+# The QML types in types.h exist only on Android.
+if (ANDROID)
+    target_sources(dateandtimeplugin PRIVATE types.h)
+endif()
 
 ecm_target_qml_sources(dateandtimeplugin SOURCES
     DatePopup.qml
